N2  - This review of 55 studies, commissioned to inform WHO guidelines, found moderate-quality evidence that tooth decay is lower when free sugars are below 10% of energy. At least one link between sugar and decay appeared in 42 of 50 child studies and all 5 adult studies, while evidence for a further benefit below 5% was rated very low quality.
N1  - Systematic review commissioned to inform WHO guidelines, following PRISMA with GRADE assessment. Of 5,990 papers, 55 studies were eligible: 3 intervention, 8 cohort, 20 population and 24 cross-sectional (the DARE summary gives 21 population and 23 cross-sectional). Variability in the data limited meta-analysis. Per DARE, GRADE was applied to the cohort studies only. Moynihan PJ, Kelly SA. J Dent Res 2014;93(1):8-18, PMID 24323509, PMC3872848.. Verified 2026-10-14. Used for: nutrition.free_sugars_and_health: supports
