N2  - In trials lasting at least four weeks, eating about 4.4 g less salt a day lowered systolic blood pressure by about 4.2 mm Hg and diastolic by about 2.1 mm Hg. The fall was larger in people with high blood pressure (about 5.4 mm Hg systolic) than in those with normal blood pressure (about 2.4 mm Hg).
