N2  - This umbrella review pooled 45 analyses covering about 9.9 million people. Higher ultra-processed food intake was linked to higher risk of cardiovascular death (RR 1.50, very low certainty), type 2 diabetes (RR 1.12 in dose-response analysis, moderate certainty) and anxiety. Evidence was weaker for death from any cause (RR 1.21, low certainty), depression and obesity.
N1  - Umbrella review of epidemiological meta-analyses (mostly observational, largely prospective cohort data), with evidence-class grading (I-IV/V) plus GRADE; 45 unique pooled analyses (13 dose-response, 32 non-dose-response), n=9,888,373. BMJ 2024;384:e077310, PMID 38418082.. Verified 2026-10-14. Used for: nutrition.ultra_processed_food_associations: supports
