N2  - Three large US cohorts covered about 207,000 health professionals. People with the highest ultra-processed food intake had 17% higher risk of cardiovascular disease, 23% higher risk of coronary heart disease and 9% higher risk of stroke than those with the lowest. The authors rated the evidence from their meta-analysis as high for coronary heart disease, moderate for cardiovascular disease and low for stroke.
