N2  - Twenty weight-stable adults lived on a research ward and ate as much as they wanted. They ate about 508 kcal/day more on an ultra-processed diet than on an unprocessed diet matched for presented calories, sugar, fat, sodium and fibre. Over 2 weeks per diet, they gained 0.9 kg on the ultra-processed diet and lost 0.9 kg on the unprocessed one.
