N2  - The trial included 55 adults in England with overweight or obesity. Both 8-week diets followed UK healthy-eating guidance and led to weight loss, but less on the ultra-processed diet (-1.05% vs -2.06%). Triglycerides improved more on the minimally processed diet, whereas LDL cholesterol fell more on the ultra-processed diet.
N1  - Randomised 2x2 crossover controlled feeding trial, free-living, ad libitum, all food provided; two 8-week diets (both following the UK Eatwell Guide) with a 4-week washout; n=55 adults in England with BMI 25 to <40 and high habitual UPF intake (UPDATE trial, NCT05627570). Nat Med 2025;31(10):3297-3308, PMID 40760353.. Verified 2026-10-14. Used for: nutrition.ultra_processed_food_associations: supports
